# Adeline's power counts only creatures Bot1 controls ("you control"), so Bot2's Ornithopter adds nothing: with Bot1's own
# Ornithopter she is a 2/4. "Whenever you attack" does not need Adeline to attack: Ornithopter attacks alone, Adeline
# stays home, and the Human token still arrives tapped and attacking Bot2 (CR 508.4); Adeline is then a 3/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Adeline, Resplendent Cathar
Ornithopter
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Power = 2
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Ornithopter > Bot2; Human Token > Bot2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Power = 3
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Tapped = False
Bot1.Battlefield = Adeline, Resplendent Cathar; Ornithopter; Human Token
